    "repo": "swesmith/msiemens__tinydb.10644a0e",
    "problem_statement": "# LRUCache in utils.py returns incorrect values\n\n## Description\nThe `LRUCache` implementation in `tinydb/utils.py` has an issue where it returns incorrect values when retrieving items.\n\n## Steps to Reproduce\n```python\nfrom tinydb.utils import LRUCache\n\n# Create a cache\ncache = LRUCache(5)\n\n# Add some items\ncache['key1'] = 'value1'\ncache['key2'] = 'value2'\n\n# Try to retrieve items\nprint(cache['key1'])  # Should return 'value1' but returns 'key1' instead\nprint(cache['key2'])  # Should return 'value2' but returns 'key2' instead\n\n# Try to access a non-existent key\nprint(cache['nonexistent'])  # Should raise KeyError but returns None instead\n```\n\n## Expected Results\n- When retrieving an existing key, the cache should return the associated value\n- When trying to access a non-existent key, a KeyError should be raised\n\n## Actual Results\n- When retrieving an existing key, the cache returns the key itself instead of the value\n- When trying to access a non-existent key, it returns None instead of raising a KeyError\n\nThis breaks the expected behavior of a dictionary-like object and can cause subtle bugs in code that uses the LRUCache."
  },
